READING
  * Every model obeys the identical per-branch counting law (s and s+4).
  * The observable spectral-edge exponent (w -> 0) is s if the base branch has non-zero amplitude and
    s+4 if it vanishes; on any finite window the effective exponent interpolates (non-integer values
    such as the record's +2.216 shift are of this kind). The amplitude ratio is supplied, so the
    counting law SELECTS AMONG classes (CON) and does not FIX the edge exponent.
